      results. What matters is showing clearly how it affects you on most days.
  - question: I can do things sometimes. Should I say I can do them?
    answer: >-
      Only say you can do something if you can do it safely, to a good enough
      standard, as often as you need to and in a reasonable time. If doing it
      causes a lot of pain, takes you much longer, or leaves you exhausted
      afterwards, explain that. This is the law, not a trick.
